@div proverb 4.57

B.4.57.32. piriŋ-e e₂ ni₂-te-na-ka-da du₃-a ab#-la₂-la₂
#lem: piriŋ[lion]; e[house]; ni[self]; du[build]; la[hang]
#tr.en: The lion is tied up with (?) that of which his own house is made. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.57.32

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.58

B.4.58.33. lu₂-IM ib₂-dab₅-ba lu₂ gen₆-na ba-an#-dim₂
#lem: lutumu[criminal]; dab[seize]; lu[person]; gin[confirm]; dim[create]
#tr.en: That which the thief has taken was made by an honest man. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.58.33

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.59

B.4.59.34. ki ab-kal# diŋir#-ra-kam sahar-ra-am₃ bi₂-ib₂-šu₂-šu₂-un
#lem: ki[place]; kal[rare]; diŋir[deity]; sahar[soil]; šuš[cover]
#tr.en: To appreciate the earth is for the gods; I am merely covered in dust. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.59.34

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.60

B.4.60.35. zig₃-ga saŋ niŋ₂-gur₁₁-ra-ka bid₃ ab-gu₅-ul
#lem: zig[rise]; saŋ[head]; niŋgur[property]; bed[anus]; gal[big]
#tr.en: In respect of both expenditures and capital goods, the anus is well supplied. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.60.35

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.61

B.4.61.36. nam-sis-a bid₃ ib-ra ka ba-an-kur₉
#lem: namsesa[bitterness]; bed[anus]; rah[beat]; kag[mouth]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: Bitterness afflicted the anus; but it entered by way of the mouth. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.61.36

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.62

B.4.62.37. gu-du-e# še₁₀ dur₂-e dug₄-ge inim# dirig#-ge am₃-ta-ab-tum₃
#lem: gudu[buttocks]; šed[excrement]; dur[buttocks]; dug[speak]; inim[word]; dirig[make more than]; tum[bring]
#tr.en: The anus breaks wind; talking produces excessive words. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.4.62.37

@end proverb

@div proverb 4.63

B.4.63.38. ama sikil#-sikil#-la ma₂-addir#-ra a nu-tuku-me-en
#lem: ama[mother]; sikil[pure]; maʾaddir[ferryboat]; a[water]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: O …… mother, I have no water in the ferry-boat. 
